Relevant columns and their roles  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_TIMESERIES."GEO_ID": restrict the series to the state of California (geoId/06).  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_TIMESERIES."DATE": pick only the 2023 observation dates.  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_TIMESERIES."VARIABLE": identify the exact indicators (past‑due, forbearance, foreclosure, etc.).  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_TIMESERIES."VALUE": percentage share that each indicator represents.  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_ATTRIBUTES."VARIABLE_GROUP": tells whether the variable measures 90‑180‑day past‑due, forbearance, or foreclosure / bankruptcy / deed‑in‑lieu.  
• FHFA_MORTGAGE_PERFORMANCE_ATTRIBUTES."MARKET": let us focus on “Overall Market” (statewide portfolio).  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑answer queries (all limited to 20 rows) that can be run in Snowflake; every identifier is wrapped in double quotes.

